.TH SIBILLA 1 "2026-08-19" "SibillaOS" "SibillaOS Manual"
.SH NAME
sibilla \- administer the SibillaOS LLM appliance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sibilla
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sibilla
is the single entry point for administering a SibillaOS machine: an
Ubuntu-based system that serves local language models through one
authenticated, OpenAI-compatible API on port 8080. Every subcommand
is also installed as a standalone
.BI sibilla\- COMMAND
executable.
.PP
The machine serves what it honestly runs: model selection at first
boot picks a model that fits the detected hardware, and models past
the machine's RAM are refused rather than attempted. Larger models
(the "large" catalog tier) are strictly opt-in.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS sibilla setup [\-\-model MODEL_ID] [\-\-engine ollama|vllm]
Turn an already-installed Ubuntu machine into the appliance without
reinstalling the OS: detect the hardware, install the pinned inference
engine if missing, select and download a model, bring up the
authenticated gateway. Run as root.
.B \-\-model
overrides the auto-selected model;
.B \-\-engine
forces the engine instead of detecting it. This path is a guest on an
existing system: it does not touch the firewall and does not enable
the apt source on its own.
.SS sibilla status
Health view of the whole stack: engine service state, served models
straight from the engine, disk usage of the model store, GPU and (for
a loaded large model) the real GPU/CPU layer placement, gateway
reachability in the configured mode. Exits nonzero when the engine or
the gateway is down, so it doubles as a machine check.
.SS sibilla model SUBCOMMAND
Model lifecycle against the signed curated catalog.
.TP
.B list
Curated models that fit this machine, large models with the RAM each
needs, embedding models, and llmfit recommendations for the detected
hardware.
.TP
.BI use " MODEL_ID"
Download (if needed), verify against the catalog digest and switch the
served model. Refuses embedding models, refuses large models below the
RAM floor (fail closed, before any download, no override), and states
the cost of a large model that does fit.
.TP
.BI pull " MODEL_ID"
Download and digest-verify without switching what is served; how
embedding models arrive.
.TP
.BI import " FILE " [\-\-use]
Bring a model in from a GGUF file (USB stick, shared drive) instead of
the network. The file is identified and verified by its sha256 against
the signed catalog; anything unknown is refused, with no override.
With
.B \-\-use
the imported model becomes the served model, subject to the same
guards as
.BR use .
.TP
.BI rm " MODEL_ID"
Remove a downloaded model (refuses the served one).
.TP
.B prune
Remove every downloaded model except the served one.
.SS sibilla key SUBCOMMAND
Gateway API keys:
.B list
(names and prefixes, never the keys),
.BI add " NAME" ,
.BI revoke " NAME" ,
.B rotate
.RI [ NAME ].
New keys print once, on the last line. Changes take effect
immediately: a revoked or rotated key gets 401 on its next request.
.SS sibilla tls SUBCOMMAND
Gateway transport:
.BI enable " HOSTNAME"
serves HTTPS on port 8080 with a locally trusted certificate;
.BI enable " HOSTNAME " "\-\-acme EMAIL"
serves public HTTPS on port 443 via Let's Encrypt (the hostname must
resolve to this machine, ports 80/443 open);
.B disable
returns to plain HTTP on 8080;
.B status
shows the current mode.
.SS sibilla metrics enable|disable|status
Prometheus metrics at /metrics/gateway, behind the same bearer token
as the API. Scrape configuration and a Grafana dashboard ship in
docs/observability/ in the repository.
.SS sibilla webui enable|disable|status
Open WebUI chat interface on port 3000, as an opt-in container wired
to the local engine.
.SS sibilla mcp enable|disable|status
Model Context Protocol endpoint at /mcp, behind the same keys,
exposing the tools "chat" and "list_models" to MCP clients such as
Claude Code. Client setup in docs/mcp.md.
.SS sibilla speech enable|disable|status
Local speech-to-text at /v1/audio/transcriptions, behind the same
keys, speaking the OpenAI transcription shape (multipart "file"
field). The Whisper model arrives digest-verified from the signed
catalog. Without ffmpeg the endpoint accepts 16 kHz WAV only; with
ffmpeg installed it converts most audio formats.
.SS sibilla oidc enable ISSUER_URL CLIENT_ID [EXTERNAL_URL] | disable | status
OIDC login for the WebUI against the team's own provider (Entra,
Keycloak, Google, ...). The client secret is read from stdin, never
from arguments. Protects the WebUI only: API clients keep their bearer
keys. The provider must allow EXTERNAL_URL/oauth2/callback as a
redirect URI.
.SS sibilla apply [FILE] | export | check
Configuration as code. A profile file (plain KEY=value: MODEL, TLS,
METRICS, MCP, WEBUI; every key optional) declares the desired state;
.B apply
converges the machine onto it idempotently, running only the commands
that close a gap.
.B export
prints the current state as a profile.
.B check
audits without changing: drift against the declared profile, a
hand-edited gateway configuration, the served model's digest, key file
permissions; exits nonzero on findings, so it works as a cron or fleet
probe. API keys never enter profiles. Details in docs/configuration.md.
.SS sibilla connect [\-\-write|\-\-env|\-\-mcp|\-\-snippet python|node|\-\-remote]
Client configuration for editors, agents and SDKs. Without flags,
prints the full connection kit.
.B \-\-write
places Continue and aider configurations (with backups);
.B \-\-env
emits .env lines for any OpenAI SDK;
.B \-\-mcp
emits the claude mcp add command, key filled in;
.B \-\-snippet
emits SDK boilerplate;
.B \-\-remote
emits a self-contained script for a developer workstation that prompts
for the key on stdin, never argv or shell history.
.SS sibilla bench
Measure the machine through the authenticated gateway, so the numbers
are what a client experiences: time to first token and generation
speed, median of three runs, printed as a paste-ready markdown table
on stdout.
.SS sibilla doctor
Paste-ready diagnostic report for bug reports. Contains no secrets:
keys are never printed and the whole report is scrubbed of every
configured key before it reaches the terminal.
.SS sibilla remove [\-\-yes]
Clean, reversible teardown. Removes only what SibillaOS put on the
machine: a pre-existing ollama is left alone and a Caddy configuration
saved at setup time is restored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/llmd/
Machine state: engine, model, gateway.conf, profile, apikey (and
additional keys), feature toggles.
.TP
.I /usr/share/llmd/models.json
The curated model catalog, with its detached GPG signature next to it.
A catalog that fails signature verification is refused.
.TP
.I /var/lib/llmd/models/
The model store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, or when stdout is not a terminal, all output is plain text
with no escape sequences; piped output is byte-stable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Commands exit 0 on success and nonzero on failure.
.B sibilla status
and
.B sibilla apply check
exit nonzero on findings by design.
.SH SEE ALSO
Repository and documentation:
.I https://github.com/engineering87/sibillaos
(docs/configuration.md, docs/airgap.md, docs/embeddings.md,
docs/large-models.md, docs/mcp.md).
